          "instructions": "Contact centre is 24x7 (\"Toll free 7x24 help line\"); the same two numbers serve calls from abroad — report the loss, answer the security questions, and the card is blocked with a ticket number issued. Any SBI branch can hotlist the card on a written request. Netbanking: SBI pages link \"TO BLOCK DEBIT CARD\" to https://retail.onlinesbi.sbi/retail/blockatmcardintermediate.htm. No SMS block format is published for debit cards — the \"ATM <ticket no>\" SMS to 567676 only tracks ATM-complaint tickets. Same numbers appear as 1800 11 2211 and 1800 425 3800 on the contact page; number2 1800 11 1109 is the line for reporting unauthorised electronic transactions (also 94491 12211 mobile, toll free, and 080-2659 9990 chargeable). E-mail customercare@sbi.co.in.",
